      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:
-	Windows
-	Exterior doors
-	Lights fixtures
-	Receptacles
-	Electrical panel
-	Basement and crawl space
-	Wood stove
-	Heating ducts
-	Furnace combustion air supply

Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings. You can receive a 5000$ rebate to increase the air sealing of your building. In order to receive the rebate, the final infiltration test should reach 1.5 air changing per hour (ACH).
</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-12. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for a 12 000$ rebate for the above grade exterior walls with the addition of a minimum of R-20 over the existing insulation level. </mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the time of the audit, the insulation level of the attic was estimated to be R-40. You are eligible for a 2 500$ rebate for attic insulation for the addition of a minimum of R-20 over the existing insulation level.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>FOUNDATION
Most of the heat loss in a home comes from the basement. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  You are eligible to a 12000$ rebate for below grade wall with the addition of a minimum of R-20 over the existing insulation level.

CRAWL SPACE
We strongly recommend adding insulation on the walls, the header joist (perimeter joist) and the floor above the crawl space. You are eligible to a 2000$ rebate for the addition of a minimum of R-20.
</foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled. You can receive a 120$/windows for a maximum of 1800$.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <AdditionalComments>You can visit the Good Energy program to learn more about all offered rebate and programs by following the link below:
https://yukon.ca/en/buildings-and-homes 
</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
